 "_about": "NCAA men's tournament bids for all 27 conferences we cover, by the league as it was that season. auto = conference tournament champion; at_large = teams the committee picked, First Four included. 2020 had no tournament. A league missing from a season had no bid that year (the American before it formed in 2013-14; the Ivy League, which did not play in 2020-21). Renamed leagues carry their old record: Metro = the MAAC (renamed July 2026), UAC = the WAC (renamed July 2026), CAA = the Colonial, SoCon = the Southern Conference. The Pac-12 is the exception: the old Pac-12 was a power league and the rebuilt one shares only Oregon State and Washington State with it, so its row counts the at-large bids its nine current members earned in whatever league they were in (auto left blank). Compiled from each year's Wikipedia bracket seed tables (Berth type column), read Nov 14, 2026 for the first six leagues and Nov 22, 2026 for the rest; the Nov 22 read matched all 96 league-seasons of the first six.",
 "notes": {"metro": "The MAAC until July 2026.", "uac": "The WAC until July 2026.", "american": "Formed in 2013-14, so its record starts with the 2014 tournament.", "ivy": "Did not play in 2020-21.", "pac12": "Rebuilt in 2026, so this row counts the at-large bids its nine members earned in their old leagues (mostly the Mountain West and WCC). No auto bid shown."},
